# Wave scheduler queue — one job per line. Copy this file and edit.
#
# Format:  <model_id>  <mode>  [library]  [wave_size]  [queue]
#   model_id  : the model to run (its SIF must be at /shared/sif-files/<model_id>.sif)
#   mode      : ersilia | singularity
#   library   : full name or alias (real, molport, coconut, hit, liquid);
#               optional -> falls back to the driver's default_library arg
#   wave_size : 1..1000  (optional -> default 1000)
#   queue     : SLURM partition (optional -> default cpu-queue)
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' (even indented) are ignored.
# Jobs run top-to-bottom, one at a time; the next starts when the previous finishes.

# --- examples (edit / delete) ---
eos4k4f_v1          ersilia      Enamine_Real_Sample_1.4B
eos2r5a             ersilia      Coconut_715K
mtb-public-models   singularity  molport                    500
# uses the driver's default_library (pass it as arg 2 to run-model-queue.sh):
# eos3b5e           ersilia
